{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KZrtEDQmHLRYaA4XfGWqqB","type":"tool_result","content":"66:namespace MOSPFormalization\n67-\n68:namespace Complex\n69-\n70-/-- A net–gate matrix (Möhring 1990, p. 18): `conn n g` means entry `(n, g)` is\n71-`1`, i.e. net `n` is connected to gate `g`. Rows are nets, columns gates. -/\n--\n75:variable {N Gt : Type*} [Fintype N] [DecidableEq N] [Fintype Gt] [DecidableEq Gt]\n76-\n77:namespace NetGateMatrix\n78-\n79:variable (M : NetGateMatrix N Gt) [DecidableRel M.conn]\n80-\n81-/-! ### Definitions from the source -/\n82-\n--\n111:def netGraph : SimpleGraph N where\n112-  Adj n n' := n ≠ n' ∧ ∃ g, M.conn n g ∧ M.conn n' g\n113-  symm := ⟨fun _ _ ⟨hne, g, h₁, h₂⟩ => ⟨hne.symm, g, h₂, h₁⟩⟩\n114-  loopless := ⟨fun _ ⟨hne, _⟩ => hne rfl⟩\n--\n130:theorem netGraph_eq_mospGraph : M.netGraph = M.toMOSP.mospGraph := by\n131-  ext n n'\n132-  rfl\n133-\n--\n323:theorem tracks_eq_pathwidth_add_one (hreq : ∃ n g, M.conn n g) :\n324-    M.tracks = pathwidth M.netGraph + 1 := by\n325-  rw [M.tracks_eq_mospValue hreq, M.netGraph_eq_mospGraph]\n326-  exact M.toMOSP.mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one hreq\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n\n/-! ### The game (Kirousis & Papadimitriou 1985, p. 181) -/\n\n/-- A move: place a searcher on a node, or delete the searcher of a node. -/\ninductive SearchMove (V : Type*)\n  | place (v : V)\n  | remove (v : V)\n\n/-- A position of the game: the guarded nodes and the contaminated edges. -/\nstructure SearchState (V : Type*) where\n  guards : Finset V\n  contaminated : Set (Sym2 V)\n\n/-- The guard set after a move. -/\n\nend IntervalModel\n\n/-- `H` is an interval graph: it has an interval model (in `ℕ`). -/\ndef IsIntervalGraph (H : SimpleGraph V) : Prop :=\n  Nonempty (IntervalModel ℕ H)\n\n/-- The **interval thickness** `θ(G)`: the smallest clique number of an\ninterval supergraph of `G` on the same vertice